WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:08.080
- [Mark] Okay, Elizabeth,
where'd you grow up,

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:09.830
where are you from originally?

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:11.080
- [Elizabeth] Originally, I'm from Ohio

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.200
and I was raised here in Clarksburg.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.800
- [Mark] Clarksburg, West Virginia?

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:15.720
- [Elizabeth] Mm-hm.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:16.553
- [Mark] Tell me about your childhood.

00:00:16.553 --> 00:00:18.895
You had both your parents as a kid?

00:00:18.895 --> 00:00:20.950
- Well, my mom and my dad,

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:24.317
but my dad was in and out basically.

00:00:25.895 --> 00:00:27.234
- [Mark] When you say
your dad was in and out,

00:00:27.234 --> 00:00:29.160
meaning he was...

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:30.940
- He ended up getting put in jail

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:33.530
and so my mom had us for most of the time.

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:36.470
And he tried to push
himself back in our life,

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:38.300
but we didn't really
understand why he left

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.040
in the first place, so we
didn't really want anything

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:41.873
to do with him.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:45.120
- [Mark] And how was life with your mom?

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:48.640
- It wasn't really life, it was...

00:00:51.126 --> 00:00:53.582
It sucked, it really did.

00:00:53.582 --> 00:00:57.050
- [Mark] What kind of stuff was going on?

00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:00.090
- My mom, she was hooked
on coke really bad

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:02.840
and her and her boyfriend,
they started selling it

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:06.150
and everything and I got involved with it,

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:08.173
so young I started using.

00:01:10.045 --> 00:01:12.263
- [Mark] At what age did you start?

00:01:12.263 --> 00:01:13.096
- 12.

00:01:13.096 --> 00:01:17.720
- [Mark] 12, did you finish high school?

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:18.553
- No.

00:01:18.553 --> 00:01:22.063
- [Mark] No, how far
did you get in school?

00:01:23.248 --> 00:01:24.081
- 10th.

00:01:24.081 --> 00:01:25.193
- [Mark] 10th grade?
- Yeah.

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:28.563
- [Mark] And where'd you go
after you left your mom's house?

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.030
- I got put in...

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:35.110
I've been in and out of
foster home and placements

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:35.943
and stuff like that.

00:01:35.943 --> 00:01:37.308
I got taken from her.

00:01:37.308 --> 00:01:40.133
- [Mark] Oh, at what age?

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:43.930
- Well, the first time,
I think I was eight

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:45.570
and I got put in a foster home.

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:47.710
And then my dad got me out,

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:50.583
and then that's when he dropped
me off here in Clarksburg.

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:53.730
- [Mark] What do you
mean he dropped you off?

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:56.363
- He ended up going to
jail for credit card theft,

00:01:57.970 --> 00:01:59.343
but he didn't tell anybody
he was going to jail.

00:01:59.343 --> 00:02:03.667
He just dropped us off at
Thanksgiving to my mom.

00:02:03.667 --> 00:02:07.676
- [Mark] So then what happened from there?

00:02:07.676 --> 00:02:09.200
- From there...

00:02:13.916 --> 00:02:18.430
It's foggy, but she
just didn't really care.

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:19.600
She didn't know how to raise us.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:20.703
She wasn't a good mom.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:26.760
But her boyfriend, well,
I grew up, he's my dad.

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:32.270
I seen him as my dad and he
ended up turning into somebody

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:34.453
that I didn't even know.

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:36.730
- [Mark] Any abuse or anything like that?

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:39.220
- Yeah, well, not when I was young,

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:41.163
but when I got older, yeah.

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:44.870
My mom knew about it,
she let me go over there

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:49.080
and stuff like that and
yeah, stuff happened.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:49.913
- [Mark] Sexual abuse?

00:02:49.913 --> 00:02:50.746
- Yeah.

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:54.780
- [Mark] So you left home at what age?

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.340
So you were in the foster system,

00:02:58.340 --> 00:02:59.930
but you were going back and forth to home?

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:01.610
- Yeah, well, yeah.

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:03.540
And when I was staying with
my mom, I ended up getting put

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:05.670
in placement for truancy.

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:10.050
And then I got out of placement

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:15.050
and just kept going back and
forth and some stuff happened

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:19.910
with more sexual abuse
and I had to go testify

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:21.400
and my mom lied on the stand.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:26.400
And somebody else, the
state let them take me in

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:28.550
and they ended up kicking me out

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:30.783
and I got put back in placement.

00:03:33.522 --> 00:03:35.293
- [Mark] And so today you're living where?

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:37.470
- Everywhere.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:39.100
- [Mark] You're just drifting?

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:39.933
- Mm-hm.

00:03:40.994 --> 00:03:42.400
- [Mark] Are you using drugs as well?

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:43.400
- Yes.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.250
- [Mark] Which is your drug?

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:46.897
- Meth, I'm an IV user.

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:50.740
- [Mark] And what do you do for money now?

00:03:53.787 --> 00:03:58.690
- I tried the middleman stuff
and sell to other people

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:02.040
and I wouldn't call it prostituting,

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:05.453
but I more or less, men.

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:08.450
I basically flirt with
men, finesse them and stuff

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:12.880
and help me, but that's the
only people who wanna help me

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:14.030
seems like are men.

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:14.863
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:04:16.868 --> 00:04:17.820
And do you have kids of your own?

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:18.783
- Yes.

00:04:18.783 --> 00:04:19.616
- [Mark] How many kids do you have?

00:04:19.616 --> 00:04:21.427
- I have two little girls.

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:22.840
- [Mark] And you're
raising your daughters?

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:24.060
- No.

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:25.103
- [Mark] Where are they?

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:31.023
- Both of them are in the foster family.

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:34.590
- [Mark] Do you have any
contact with them at all?

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:35.540
- No.
- [Mark] No.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:43.600
So do you have any friends
here in the street,

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:46.433
do have anyone you trust
or anyone you're close to?

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:49.250
- No, not...

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:51.210
No, definitely not.

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:56.210
There are this couple,
they've helped me out a lot.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:59.020
They're a big part of my life,

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:02.780
but they basically sell drugs, too,

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:05.300
so still the dope game,
you can't trust nobody.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.930
- [Mark] Yeah, you been arrested before?

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:08.880
- Yeah.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:09.800
- [Mark] For drugs?

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:14.663
- No, for a domestic and trespassing.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:24.130
- [Mark] What are the
biggest problems or dangers

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:26.357
that you have with your lifestyle?

00:05:27.343 --> 00:05:32.343
- Being a 24-year-old woman
on the streets, it's tough.

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:37.380
Most of the problem is men

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:39.650
and people think they
can take advantage of you

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:41.713
because you're a female and you're young.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:45.367
- [Mark] What's the worse
thing that's happened to you?

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:50.223
- I've had somebody hotshot me.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.880
I had them work up my shot down at GoMart,

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:56.470
and next thing you know
I ended up doing it,

00:05:56.470 --> 00:05:58.030
I woke up with my pants down

00:05:58.030 --> 00:06:00.720
and I was laying right beside GoMart.

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:04.030
- [Mark] I'm sorry, somebody shot you?

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:05.880
- Yeah, I had them work up my shot

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:10.880
and they basically put heroin
and meth in it together

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:12.310
and hotshotted me out of it.

00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:13.143
- [Mark] Oh, a hotshot.

00:06:13.143 --> 00:06:14.333
- Yeah.
- [Mark] Oh, I see.

00:06:16.003 --> 00:06:17.210
- [Mark] Have you OD'd before?

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:19.583
- Yeah, three times, yeah.

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:24.510
- [Mark] Where do you see
your life going from here?

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:26.610
You're 24 and what do you see happening

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:27.960
in the next five, 10 years?

00:06:29.289 --> 00:06:31.380
- I don't see anything happening.

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:34.070
I don't know what my future is.

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:36.240
I want better, I've tried to do better

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:40.410
but the streets just
keep coming back to it.

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:42.486
- [Mark] Yeah, it's almost
like you're addicted to this.

00:06:42.486 --> 00:06:43.319
- Yeah.

00:06:43.319 --> 00:06:46.360
- [Mark] Yeah, do you see the connection

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:47.700
between what happened to you as a kid

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:49.903
and where you are today?

00:06:50.966 --> 00:06:55.690
- [Elizabeth] Yeah, 'cause
if honestly it wasn't for all

00:06:55.690 --> 00:06:58.150
of this happening, I wouldn't
become the person I am today

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:01.900
and probably a lot worse

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.750
if everything that happened this way.

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:07.180
I could be dead or something else.

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:08.450
- [Mark] Do you get depressed?

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:09.530
- [Elizabeth] Oh yeah.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:10.883
- [Mark] You been suicidal before?

00:07:10.883 --> 00:07:12.833
- [Elizabeth] Yeah.
- [Mark] You have.

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:16.960
What kind of stuff have you considered?

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:21.440
- [Elizabeth] Well, I had to
get my stomach pumped once

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:24.760
for I took a whole bottle
of my seizure medication

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:26.150
when I was younger.

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:29.470
My mom watched me grab the
bottle out of her cabinet.

00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:32.320
And she asked me what I
was doing and I told her

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:35.443
and she started cussing me and everything.

00:07:35.443 --> 00:07:37.957
And I went in the bedroom
and I just walked in

00:07:38.973 --> 00:07:41.650
and from there, it's blank.

00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:43.800
I woke up three days
later in the hospital.

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:48.840
- [Mark] Have you considered
getting a therapist

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:50.140
and talking this stuff out?

00:07:50.140 --> 00:07:52.370
- [Elizabeth] I've had
therapists all my life.

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:53.830
I don't see talking to somebody

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:56.350
who hasn't been through
what I've been through

00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:57.650
helpful at all.

00:07:57.650 --> 00:07:59.200
I feel like they're judging me.

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:03.793
- [Mark] When was the
worst point of your life?

00:08:05.070 --> 00:08:06.420
- Now.
- [Mark] Right now?

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:12.260
- I'd rather relive
everything I did as a child,

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:16.090
it's bad to say, than do
what I'm going through now.

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:17.725
- [Mark] But if you had
two parents that loved you

00:08:17.725 --> 00:08:18.820
and supported you and all that,

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:21.363
you feel like you'd be
in a different space?

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:25.543
- If I had two totally
different parents, yeah.

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:32.134
- [Mark] And in some ways,

00:08:32.134 --> 00:08:34.210
it's almost like you're
repeating the cycle.

00:08:34.210 --> 00:08:35.670
- Oh yeah, every day I wake up,

00:08:35.670 --> 00:08:38.800
I wonder where I'm gonna lay my head,

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:41.250
how I'm gonna get money to feed myself.

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:43.960
There's days I go without
eating, not because I'm on meth

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:46.020
but because I can't afford to eat.

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:46.853
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:51.910
You ever been in love before?

00:08:51.910 --> 00:08:52.743
- Yeah.

00:08:56.960 --> 00:08:59.083
- [Mark] Does this lifestyle
get in the way of that?

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:03.000
- Well, me being homeless

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:04.850
and not really having anything, yeah.

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:14.203
- [Mark] What do you think

00:09:14.203 --> 00:09:16.677
would help you the most right now?

00:09:17.935 --> 00:09:22.935
- If someone could just
help me and not doubt me.

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:27.130
People doubting me is the
worst 'cause it gives me

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:29.363
in my head to where I feel like I can't,

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:32.780
but I know I can do better.

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:39.727
'Cause I don't see a point
in trying to get better

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:43.993
and trying if I don't really
have anything to live for.

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:48.903
- [Mark] Yeah, losing your kids

00:09:48.903 --> 00:09:50.730
has gotta set you back, right?

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:52.138
Is that what gets to you the most?

00:09:52.138 --> 00:09:53.386
- Yeah.

00:09:53.386 --> 00:09:55.719
- [Mark] It's gotta be hard.

00:09:58.878 --> 00:10:03.500
And then your unstable housing

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:06.713
has gotta be difficult to deal with, too.

00:10:07.802 --> 00:10:12.740
- If I had my own place, I
definitely wouldn't be like this.

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:16.390
I mean, I just wanna be able to...

00:10:16.390 --> 00:10:18.753
I don't even know the
last time I laid in a bed.

00:10:20.182 --> 00:10:21.015
- [Mark] Where do you typically sleep,

00:10:21.015 --> 00:10:23.331
or with crystal meth, you don't sleep?

00:10:23.331 --> 00:10:25.820
- Well, I mean, eventually
you have to sleep,

00:10:25.820 --> 00:10:27.220
yeah, but I do.

00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:32.220
I just usually a guy's
house I have to stay at

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:34.623
and I'm too scared to fall asleep.

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:40.520
But when my parents,
they're not my real parents,

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:42.590
but they're my street parents,

00:10:42.590 --> 00:10:43.700
they have their own life to live, too.

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:48.463
I can't go there and sleep whenever.

00:10:51.468 --> 00:10:52.660
- [Mark] Do you have
any dreams or anything

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:55.773
that you'd love to see happen for yourself

00:10:55.773 --> 00:10:57.253
or are you just trying to survive?

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:03.220
- Both, I mean, I just want to be able

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:04.430
to have something of my own.

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:06.710
I wanna be able to say
I accomplished something

00:11:06.710 --> 00:11:08.470
and something good, instead of...

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:12.730
But yeah, I'm just trying to survive.

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:17.423
- [Mark] Yeah, and there's
a lot of shame in this.

00:11:18.340 --> 00:11:20.390
You feel guilty for losing
your kids, you feel guilty

00:11:20.390 --> 00:11:24.859
for some of the things you do.

00:11:24.859 --> 00:11:25.942
- Yeah, yeah.

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:33.223
I should've known the way
I grew up with my mom.

00:11:35.143 --> 00:11:35.976
As soon as I had my kid,

00:11:35.976 --> 00:11:36.844
I was like, yeah, I know what to do,

00:11:36.844 --> 00:11:39.110
I know how to raise her and everything.

00:11:39.110 --> 00:11:42.257
And I didn't.

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:44.880
- [Mark] What do you think it is?

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:47.320
Do you think it's just that
your self worth gets set

00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:50.290
at a low point because of what
you went through as a kid,

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:51.890
having the mom you did, having a stepdad

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:54.800
that did what he did?

00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:59.290
- In a way, it makes me
stronger, but with all my...

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:04.230
I have a lot of mental issues
and that gets in the way.

00:12:04.230 --> 00:12:08.923
That got in the way of me being
a mother and everyday life.

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:18.307
- [Mark] What's the hardest part for you?

00:12:22.890 --> 00:12:27.850
- [Elizabeth] Being alone,
knowing that there's nobody

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:29.543
that really cares, nobody.

00:12:37.450 --> 00:12:39.050
- [Mark] All right,
Elizabeth, thank you so much

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:42.534
for talking with me and I wish you luck

00:12:42.534 --> 00:12:45.270
getting your life together.

00:12:45.270 --> 00:12:46.165
- Thank you.

00:12:46.165 --> 00:12:47.577
- [Mark] You could use
some nice breaks, right?

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:50.493
Thank you.

